--- !u!114 &180311901
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 180311900}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1c9aeab9b26edec439c60251089cbdfc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  enlistButton: {fileID: 738716976}
  runAwayButton: {fileID: 1412201787}
  continueButton: {fileID: 366060219}
  endingTextObject: {fileID: 170412804}
  firstEndingText: "The homeland is being invaded by a hostile enemy nation. They
    are here to steal resources and, most importantly, the red balls. If they\u2019re
    able to win, they will strip all the citizens of all their hard-earned red balls
    they have collected throughout their entire life. You cannot let this happen.
    \\n\\n\\nWill you enlist in the military and defend the homeland against the
    evil aggressors? Or disobey and run away?"
  ending1Texts:
  - "You choose to do as you are told. You join the military and prepare to fight
    for your country. With the enemies at the doorstep, there\u2019s no time for
    sufficient training and you\u2019re given no more information than what you were
    initially told. You\u2019re handed a rifle and sent out to the front lines."
  - "The fighting is brutal and confusing. Your homeland\u2019s army is disorganised
    and poorly prepared. The enemy feels to be everywhere. Their motive is unclear
    to you, all you know is that they want to take away your hard earned life. A
    large counteroffensive is ordered, and in the charge, you are shot and killed."
  - You fought for your life, for your homeland, and for the red balls. But most
    importantly, you fought because you were told to. You will never know the outcome
    of the war, and you will never know if you made the right choice.
  ending2Texts:
  - "You choose to disobey and make a run for it. You don\u2019t know what is really
    happening, but there\u2019s one thing you do know for sure: you aren\u2019t willing
    to die for the red balls. The soldiers could probably catch you if they tried,
    but they have too many other things to worry about right now."
  - You go into hiding, first in the recesses of the city before eventually making
    it out to the countryside. Keeping a low profile is essential, desertion comes
    with a heavy price. The war never seems to make it to the city, so hopefully
    you can eventually return to your home.
  - "It\u2019s impossible to know if you made the right decision, and there\u2019s
    a lot of things you don\u2019t understand, but there are a few things you can
    be sure of. You don\u2019t trust what you\u2019ve been told, you don\u2019t trust
    the red balls, and most importantly, you\u2019re alive. You will not die for
    anything you don\u2019t support, and because of that, you still have a life ahead
    of you."
